codex
The launcher failure is caused by the container’s PID/proc mismatch: `/proc/self` points to a host PID that is not visible in the mounted proc tree, and Lean 4.22 uses `/proc/<pid>/exe` to locate its installation. I’m testing an in-scope local PID namespace/proc mount workaround; it changes no project files or toolchain configuration.
exec
/bin/bash -lc 'command -v unshare || true; unshare --pid --fork --mount-proc /opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0/bin/lean --version || true; command -v bwrap || true' in /workspace
 succeeded in 0ms:
/usr/bin/unshare
unshare: unshare failed: Operation not permitted

